The word pairs (/usr/lib/tactus/share/phosh-osk-stevia/word-pairs.txt)

Which word follows which, and how often, for the 10,000 commonest words:
counted by tools/tactus-word-pairs.py in Tatoeba's English sentences
(https://tatoeba.org), from its weekly export of 2026-11-21
(https://downloads.tatoeba.org/exports/per_language/eng/eng_sentences.tsv.bz2),
every twentieth sentence left out for the checks. A pair seen fewer than six
times is not kept. The file holds counts only, no sentence.

Tatoeba's exports carry no version, so the file is kept in the package's
sources rather than fetched: running the script on a newer export gives
somewhat different counts.

